% Approved behavior specification for notes.py and resources.json.
% Prepared directly after PDD provider startup was blocked. No completed sync is claimed.

Implement NotesCatalog for the existing Python standard-library Reading Room.
The versioned registry identifies shared LaTeX topics, PDF/source/code assets,
and edition-specific book-section locators. Human-authored mathematical content
and historical files remain authoritative; never regenerate them incidentally.

Public interface: NotesCatalog(repo: Path, artifacts: Path, references: dict | None),
resolve(asset_id) -> Path, evidence() -> dict, public(book_catalog) -> dict;
input_hashes(repo) -> dict[path, sha256]; outside_repo(repo, path) -> Path.

R1 MUST resolve only registered asset IDs beneath their configured resolved
repository/artifacts roots. Reject traversal and symlink escapes. Missing
optional repositories, PDFs and reports are visibly unavailable.
R2 MUST return valid indexed book locators with exact/estimated page labels.
Missing books must not make the notes catalog unusable or fabricate a locator.
R3 MUST distinguish source availability, build currency, numerical evidence,
symbolic evidence and personal learning progress. A current execution record
needs matching code/derivation/registry hashes. A current PDF additionally needs
its matching output hash. Missing, corrupt or stale reports never imply success.
R4 MUST NOT execute code, launch containers, compile LaTeX, write personal state,
or expose arbitrary repository files through catalog reads.
R5 MUST retain original manuscripts and attribution; topic chapters are shared
by a thematic master and three companions, with portrait and screen outputs.

Acceptance: tests/test_notes.py and the existing tests/test_server.py. Exercise
actual HTTP/source responses, book mappings, missing external roots, modified
code invalidating evidence, replaced PDFs and registered symlink escapes.
